spes USB file server (0187): ios-flame 0091 sweet_files.c on tcp 2223, USB link only; TX padding/ARP fix.

From NWylynko/ios-flame @ 745c4341 (ROADMAP-TREIBER.md Nachtrag 1): one request per connection,
PUT/GET/MKDIR/LINK/RM/CHMOD with "OK <n>" / "ERR <errno>" replies, kernel VFS calls (vnode_open, vn_rdwr,
mkdir1at/symlinkat_internal/unlink1 through wrappers in vfs_syscalls.c), PUT sets root:wheel. Added for
spes: only peers in 192.168.7.0/24 are served (sock_getpeername), sweetusbfiles=0 leaves it off (on by
default on spes with sweetusb=2). TX path (also from 0091): ARP replies to the Ethernet broadcast
address and frames padded to 60 bytes, which macOS's ECM side needs (it drops short frames and ARP
replies unicast to its shown iMACAddress) - a likely cause of the lost live-log backlog.

